Aim:
To connect Tableau to a data source and prepare the data for creating visualizations.

Algorithm
1. Open Tableau Public.
2. Select the required data source.
3. Import the dataset.
4. Verify the imported data.
5. Perform basic data preparation.
6. Save the workbook.

Program:

 import pandas as pd
 # Load dataset
 data = pd.read_csv("sales_data.csv")
 # Display first 5 rows
 print(data.head())
 # Check for missing values
 print(data.isnull().sum())
 # Remove duplicate records
 data = data.drop_duplicates()
 # Convert Sales column to numeric
 data["Sales"] = pd.to_numeric(data["Sales"])
 # Save cleaned dataset
 data.to_csv("cleaned_sales_data.csv", index=False)
 print("Data prepared successfully.")

Program Explanation
• pandas is imported as pd.
• read csv() loads the CSV dataset.
• head() displays the first five records.
• isnull().sum() checks missing values.
• drop duplicates() removes duplicate rows.
• to numeric() converts Sales values into numeric form.
• to csv() saves the cleaned dataset.

Libraries / Functions Used
Pandas: Used for reading, cleaning, transforming and saving tabular data.

